            <div xml:id="d541">

                <pb facs="0762" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg660"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/1458: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-30T10:00:00+01:00">September 30,
                            1935—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 30—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>400. There has been circulated the following telegram dated September 28
                    addressed to the President of the Council by the Emperor of Abyssinia.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Firmly and constantly resolved upon peace Ethiopia will continue to
                        collaborate with Council for pacific settlement in accordance with the
                        Covenant. Would however draw Council’s most serious attention to increasing
                        gravity threat Italian aggression owing to continual despatch reenforcements
                        troops and other preparation despite our <pb facs="0763" n="661"
                            xml:id="pg661"/> attitude. Earnestly beg Council to take as soon as
                        possible all precautions against Italian aggression since circumstances have
                        been such that we should fail in our duty if we delayed any longer the
                        general mobilization necessary to ensure defence our country. Our
                        contemplated mobilization will not affect our previous orders to keep our
                        troops at a distance from the frontier and we confirm our resolution to
                        cooperate closely with League of Nations in all circumstances.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
